  {
    "key": "bob.workflows",
    "metadata": {
      "selective_tools_version": 1
    },
    "content": "Workflows describe methods, not tool bundles. describe_tool with a workflow name retains its method in current system instructions without loading member schemas. Load only the individual tools needed for the current subtask by exact name. Loaded methods and tool instructions survive worker restart.",
    "definition": {}
  },
  {
    "key": "tools.describe_tool",
    "metadata": {},
    "definition": {
      "description": "Select a listed workflow method or load one listed tool by exact name. Workflow selection loads no member tools. For an individual tool, its complete manual and schema appear once in the next request’s native tool definition. Previously loaded methods and tools persist for this turn.",
      "additional_description": "The result is a reference to the next request’s authoritative instructions, not a second copy of its schema. Loading grants no authority: current project policy, prerequisites and exact contracts still apply."
    }
  },
  {
    "key": "bob.toolbox.intro-lazy",
    "metadata": {},
    "definition": {},
    "content": "Your tools and colleagues\n\nThe directory lists project capabilities. describe_tool selects a workflow method without loading its members, or loads one exact tool name. Its manual and schema appear in the next request’s tool definition. Use only the tools needed for the current subtask; loaded knowledge persists for the turn. Waiting tools still need their prerequisite. The loaded manual explains any colleague’s handoff."
  },
